<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>DW - English for Africa</title><subtitle type="html">News, Analysis and Service from Germany and Europe - in 30 Languages</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:19Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-africa" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12756?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>One year on, families seek justice after election violence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2bea710a1f953722b357ece6bde9399a10f5879df2430f888e1fa59e309f8913</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:19Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T16:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/one-year-on-families-seek-justice-after-election-violence/a-79779105--19ee0afa750b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/one-year-on-families-seek-justice-after-election-violence/a-79779105?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">One year after Tanzania's deadly post-election violence, families are still seeking answers. A government inquiry recorded 518 deaths. DW research has documented apparent use of excessive force by security forces.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Egypt orders closure of independent news site Mada Masr</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5c0f67fa80e62ded9615cdcb19ab9bf8bed0fe137309aec806784e5daacb413b</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:19Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T23:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/egypt-orders-closure-of-independent-news-site-mada-masr/a-79781842--499fd97538eb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/egypt-orders-closure-of-independent-news-site-mada-masr/a-79781842?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Editor-in-chief Lina Attalah was briefly detained and fined over licensing violations. Rights groups condemned the ruling as a major blow to press freedom in Egypt, where independent media face growing pressure.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>DR Congo reports over 10,000 Ebola cases as the outbreak spreads abroad, with no approved vaccine or specific treatment for the Bundibugyo virus</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5056c70dc7a347f5996e39c25ae05c6fad11861020ce8aea31a1e4e995686af1</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:19Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T11:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/dr-congo-reports-over-10-000-ebola-cases-as-the-outbreak-spreads-abroad-with-no-approved-vaccine-or-/a-79773667--055ba7810ea4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/dr-congo-reports-over-10-000-ebola-cases-as-the-outbreak-spreads-abroad-with-no-approved-vaccine-or-specific-treatment-for-the-bundibugyo-virus/a-79773667?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">DR Congo has reported more than 10,000 Ebola cases and nearly 4,900 deaths. The outbreak involves a virus for which there is no approved vaccine or specific treatment, complicating efforts to contain its spread.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>'Tinubu Must Go!': Nigeria's northern protests test limits of political dissent</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:67de2340351693439c60ac10c604d7a9bb7bfdd5dba0c0bd981fbaff399bf7f6</id><updated>2026-10-29T06:02:19Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T14:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tinubu-must-go-nigeria-s-northern-protests-test-limits-of-political-dissent/a-79713785--b9a2ff0fa9c4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tinubu-must-go-nigeria-s-northern-protests-test-limits-of-political-dissent/a-79713785?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The arrest of several men wearing anti-government T-shirts and the disruption of a political meeting have renewed debate over free expression and protest rights in Nigeria.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
